        "code": {
          "text": "Patient-reported right dorsal forearm skin finding"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Small pea-sized dry, scaly, pink patch, noticed approximately 3–4 weeks ago; gradual onset and now somewhat rougher to touch and more visible. Colour unchanged. Patient reports no pain, itch, bleeding, ulceration, rapid growth, preceding trauma, or bite. Sorbolene may have helped slightly."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
